# Trivy Ignore Configuration for TruthBeacon
# Prepared by Orange Heart Industries • Security & Compliance Audit
#
# GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g (RUSTSEC-2024-0429):
# Unsoundness in Iterator and DoubleEndedIterator impls for glib::VariantStrIter
#
# Impact & Reachability Analysis:
# 1. Package: glib v0.18.5 (fixed in glib >= 0.20.0).
# 2. Dependency chain: Pulled transitively only on Linux targets via Tauri v2 -> wry -> tao / webkit2gtk -> gtk v0.18 -> glib v0.18.5.
# 3. Not compiled on macOS or Windows.
# 4. In Linux builds, the unsoundness is exclusively in VariantStrIter::impl_get, exposed only via Variant::array_iter_str().
# 5. TruthBeacon and Tauri's runtime never call Variant::array_iter_str() or interact with VariantStrIter.
# 6. Upgrading glib to 0.20+ is blocked upstream by Tauri v2 / wry / tao / webkit2gtk-rs ecosystem dependencies on gtk-rs 0.18.
# 7. Snoozed until Tauri upstream updates GTK-rs bindings to glib >= 0.20.0.
GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g
RUSTSEC-2024-0429

# CVE-2023-53156 (RUSTSEC-2023-0080):
# Integer overflow in transpose crate inside rustfft -> rustdct -> img_hash.
# Resolution: Patched rustfft to depend on transpose 0.2.3 (fixed version >= 0.2.3).
# Reachability Analysis:
# TruthBeacon uses fixed 8x8 (64-pixel) perceptual hashing, which never processes large slices required for integer overflow.
CVE-2023-53156
RUSTSEC-2023-0080
